# Reviewed tenant-filter bypasses. Format: repository-relative path|method-call count|why the bypass is required.
# Counts include only IgnoreQueryFilters() calls, not comments or documentation. Any count change requires review.
ProjectBeacon.API/Auth/ApiTokenAuthMiddleware.cs|9|Authenticates API tokens and resolves device, chat, task, and run ownership before tenant scope is bound; each lookup is constrained by the token or validated actor resource.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Agents/ApplyAgentConfigHandler.cs|1|Resolves the project membership needed to authorize an agent configuration apply before project scope is available.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Agents/ModelBackendHandlers.cs|2|Checks cross-project membership and role bindings while authorizing model backend changes.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Milestones/MilestoneHandlers.cs|9|Resolves explicitly requested projects and milestones across the ambient tenant filter, validates route ProjectId, then performs project membership or inherited Owner/Admin checks before listing or mutating milestone state; unauthorized callers cannot use filtered absence to bypass the explicit 403/404 contract.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Agents/ProjectMcpServerHandlers.cs|2|Loads project-scoped MCP configuration after validating the project requested by the caller.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Auth/LoginHandlers.cs|9|Accepts invite and login flows using opaque invite credentials, then validates invite, organization, and project membership relationships explicitly.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Authorization/AuthorizationService.cs|9|Implements central authorization by resolving the actor's project and organization memberships across tenant boundaries.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Chat/ChatHandlers.cs|8|Resolves chat sessions, parts, and project membership by explicit session and actor identifiers for authenticated chat operations.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/CommandCompletions.cs|17|Processes device-owned commands and associated pipeline, chat, eval, review, and ReleasePrepare state after validating command, device, project, and generation identifiers. ReleasePrepare completion resolves the exact pinned Release and Project, validates immutable Prepare/Verify evidence, then commits Candidate snapshot and official version atomically with the command completion.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/CommandRecovery.cs|1|Recovers stale pipeline work by its persisted command/session identifiers across the request tenant boundary.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/DesiredState.cs|2|Updates desired device and project-runtime revisions for the explicitly selected device or project.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/DeviceLifecycleHandlers.cs|2|Creates and maintains device identity and runtime links after validating the owning user and project references.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/DeviceLlamaSwapProxy.cs|2|Resolves the device's active project runtimes and memberships before proxying the authorized model operation.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/HarnessTokenCommands.cs|9|Authenticates harness tokens and resolves their explicit device, command, chat, task, subtask, eval, and project scopes.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/ProjectRuntimeHandlers.cs|15|Creates, attaches, detaches, and reports project runtime links after explicitly checking membership and device ownership; runtime attach/detach lock the selected project, refuse mutations while repository-using commands or pipeline/chat sessions are active, and preserve GitSync validity when LocalRoot changes.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/ProjectRuntimeResolver.cs|2|Resolves runtime assignment for a known project or device using explicit project and device identifiers.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/WorkstationCommandHandlers.cs|10|Claims, reports progress, and completes commands for an authenticated device; applies trusted-GitLand-only enqueue restrictions and validates the associated task, session, subtask, project, and command generation.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Evals/EvalPairHandler.cs|3|Loads and authorizes eval task, project membership, and pinned run state for the explicitly selected eval.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Identity/CurrentProjectLookup.cs|8|Finds the current actor's project and organization memberships before a tenant context has been selected; validates preferred project/org claims, direct project membership, and inherited organization Owner/Admin scope before tenant binding.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Identity/InviteHandlers.cs|19|Resolves and manages organization/project invitations; acceptance uses a narrow token-and-target lookup, then re-reads and mutates only in the invitation's bound tenant.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Projects/ApiTokenHandlers.cs|2|Lists and revokes API tokens by explicit token and owner identifiers, including tokens outside the default project filter.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Projects/ProjectHandlers.cs|11|Authorizes project administration and performs project-scoped dependent cleanup after loading the explicitly requested project.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Projects/ProjectQueries.cs|13|Lists projects and associated task, milestone, session, and section summaries visible to the current actor across their memberships.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Tasks/PipelineControlHandlers.cs|1|Loads review-run state by explicit task and project identifiers during a guarded pipeline control operation.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Tasks/PipelineFormHandlers.cs|5|Resolves pipeline form sessions, tasks, devices, and membership for a reply bound to an explicit project session.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Tasks/PipelineLifecycleHandlers.cs|2|Locks only the explicitly selected project row to serialize pipeline start and session launch against GitSync enqueue; native workstation selection and GitSync state are delegated to the separately reviewed ProjectGitSyncPreflight helper.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Tasks/PipelineSupport.cs|10|Builds pipeline state from commands, sessions, devices, and review runs restricted by the selected task and project identifiers.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Tasks/TaskLifecycleHandlers.cs|6|Performs task deletion and dependent cleanup across project-scoped related entities after authorizing the selected task.
ProjectBeacon.Web/Extensions/CircuitTenantRevalidation.cs|1|Revalidates the authenticated user identity across tenant boundaries when a Blazor circuit changes its active tenant.
ProjectBeacon.Infrastructure/Http/TenantIsolationMiddleware.cs|7|Resolves the authenticated tenant scope before tenant filters are activated; validates direct project membership, inherited organization Owner/Admin access, selected org claims, and project/org fallbacks before enabling EF filters and PostgreSQL RLS.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/ProjectGitSyncPreflight.cs|10|Resolves the task's pinned native workstation or safely infers a legacy owner from claimed pipeline command history; validates attachment and online state; expires stale GitSync queue intervals using PendingSince; evaluates project/device synchronization state and ensures changed LocalRoot values cannot reuse stale verification.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/ProjectGitSyncHandlers.cs|14|Serializes GitSync enqueue per project, expires and reuses/retargets active project commands, restores command state, and authorizes cancellation/read operations for exact project-scoped GitSync commands. Every cross-tenant lookup is constrained by route projectId and exact command/device identifiers.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Proposals/ProposalCommands.cs|4|Resolves proposal targets, authors, idempotency scope, and cross-tenant project/session ownership using explicit project and Actor identifiers before accepting or returning proposal state.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Proposals/RepoPatchProposalWorkflow.cs|1|Resolves the explicitly identified project-owned Actor subtask and profile grant before queuing an approved documentation patch; the query is constrained by proposal project, task, and subtask identifiers.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Tasks/PipelineReviewHandlers.cs|1|Loads the exact project row only after resolving the task through its scoped project/task filter, so the server can read the pinned ReviewCheckCommand without broadening caller-selected access.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Tasks/PipelineLandingHandlers.cs|7|Loads the org-scoped Project only by the exact ProjectId from a task/landing attempt already resolved in the project scope. These reads supply the pinned ReviewCheckCommand, Git policy, Preview audit owner, and Revert existence check; all other bypasses resolve review runs, attached GitLand-capable workstation, runtime, and audit scope by explicit task/project/device identifiers.
ProjectBeacon.Worker/Services/LandingAutomationService.cs|1|Scans pending landing attempts across tenants inside an explicitly unscoped worker tick after enabling TenantScope and PostgreSQL RLS; every project lookup is constrained to the current attempt's ProjectId.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/DeviceAutoSyncTargetsHandler.cs|7|Resolves project roots and AutoSync-eligible remote landing targets only after resolving the exact authenticated, non-revoked, AutoSync-capable device; runtime, task, session, review-run and verdict reads are each constrained by the explicit projectId/deviceId/taskId and remote landing is exposed only for the task's pinned device, Approved stage and latest successful landing Review proof.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/DeviceTaskWorkspaceBootstrapHandler.cs|7|Returns only the task pinned to the authenticated non-revoked workstation and its attached project runtime. For Hotfix tasks it independently validates the exact published Release, deployment SHA, immutable Candidate SHA/tag/version/branch, preparation workstation and project Release Management policy before exposing the deployed SHA/branch; no client-supplied path or ref is accepted.
ProjectBeacon.Application/Devices/DeviceRemoteLandingReconciliationHandler.cs|9|Reconciles a GitHub PR merge reported by the authenticated workstation only after exact device/project/runtime attachment, project AutoSync policy, task workstation pin and pipeline stage, latest approved Review verdict, latest source/tree/device/base-bound landing proof, and absence of Ready/Active/WaitingForUser sessions are checked. All bypassed tenant queries are constrained by the deviceId and exact projectId/taskId; the handler records an immutable project-scoped proof and closes only that task.
